            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a wedding pendant, then the Telugu for to invite."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: విందు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "విందు — vindu — \"a feast; a banquet\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పెళ్ళి తరువాత పెద్ద విందు జరిగింది. peḷḷi taruvāta pedda vindu jarigindi. After the wedding there was a big feast."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "విందు (vindu) ఇచ్చు, to give a feast."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "విందు (vindu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 5415 lists Telugu vindu, \"a feast, a treat\", in one entry with vinta, \"strange, new\", and Tamil viruntu, \"a feast, a guest\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
